WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.569 --> 00:00:04.471
(rousing music)

2
00:00:27.695 --> 00:00:32.800
(fire crackling)
(ambient music)

3
00:00:45.547 --> 00:00:50.585
(fortune teller speaking
in foreign language)

4
00:00:57.825 --> 00:01:01.996
(fortune teller speaking
in foreign language)

5
00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:05.265
(metal clanging)

6
00:01:05.332 --> 00:01:09.904
(fortune teller speaking
in foreign language)

7
00:01:09.971 --> 00:01:12.306
(man screaming)
(creatures screeching)

8
00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:17.444
(fortune teller speaking
in foreign language)

9
00:01:21.816 --> 00:01:22.984
(dramatic music)

10
00:01:23.051 --> 00:01:26.821
(air whooshing)
(metal clanging)

11
00:01:26.888 --> 00:01:31.458
(priest speaking in
foreign language)

12
00:01:46.574 --> 00:01:48.910
- Thou art He that took me out

13
00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.980
of my mother's womb,

14
00:01:53.748 --> 00:01:56.651
my prayer shall
be always of thee.

15
00:01:59.854 --> 00:02:01.923
I am become, as it were,

16
00:02:03.725 --> 00:02:05.459
a monster unto many.

17
00:02:08.863 --> 00:02:10.330
But my sure faith

18
00:02:11.866 --> 00:02:16.336
and trust is in thee.

19
00:02:16.804 --> 00:02:20.340
(soft tense music)

20
00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.482
(communion host breaks)

21
00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:58.278
God protect you, child.

22
00:02:59.947 --> 00:03:04.719
- Beautiful sermon, how
he talked about new life.

23
00:03:04.786 --> 00:03:06.453
(soft chuckle)

24
00:03:06.521 --> 00:03:10.558
- Mistress May, what a
blessing to see you here,

25
00:03:10.625 --> 00:03:13.861
glowing like the Virgin
Mother herself. (chuckles)

26
00:03:13.928 --> 00:03:16.597
It brings such joy to my heart.

27
00:03:16.664 --> 00:03:21.602
Aw, may the Lord bring my Seamus
and your husband home soon.

28
00:03:21.669 --> 00:03:23.104
Mm-hmm.

29
00:03:23.171 --> 00:03:27.575
(bell tolling)
God is good.

30
00:03:27.642 --> 00:03:28.710
- Thank you.

31
00:03:33.114 --> 00:03:34.682
- Blessed day, Mistress.

32
00:03:37.885 --> 00:03:38.986
(chain clinking)

33
00:03:39.053 --> 00:03:40.655
- [Anne] Won't she miss it?

34
00:03:40.722 --> 00:03:43.658
- She has plenty.
We have nothing.

35
00:03:48.896 --> 00:03:51.532
(birds chirping)
(eerie music)

36
00:03:54.869 --> 00:03:57.538
(Anne humming)

37
00:03:59.406 --> 00:04:02.242
(brooding music)

38
00:04:10.017 --> 00:04:11.686
Come Anne.

39
00:04:11.753 --> 00:04:16.758
Whatcha looking at?
(brooding music continues)

40
00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:31.271
(pensive music)
(footsteps continue plodding)

41
00:04:31.338 --> 00:04:34.142
(twine rustling)

42
00:04:35.543 --> 00:04:37.277
(Anne sniffing)
(pensive music continues)

43
00:04:37.344 --> 00:04:40.148
(seeds rattling)

44
00:04:54.461 --> 00:04:59.567
(hair rustling)

45
00:05:14.582 --> 00:05:15.482
Oh.

46
00:05:17.618 --> 00:05:18.519
Oh.

47
00:05:25.993 --> 00:05:28.830
(water sloshing)

48
00:05:33.768 --> 00:05:36.704
(knife thudding)

49
00:05:36.771 --> 00:05:39.607
(water sloshing)

50
00:05:42.076 --> 00:05:47.148
(fire crackling)
(pensive music continues)

51
00:05:52.286 --> 00:05:54.121
(fire crackling)

52
00:05:54.188 --> 00:05:55.122
Mm, mm.

53
00:05:57.625 --> 00:06:02.663
(dish clanking)
(fire crackling)

54
00:06:03.764 --> 00:06:07.034
(slurping)
- [Anne] Hmpf.

55
00:06:11.873 --> 00:06:14.709
(fire crackling)

56
00:06:15.943 --> 00:06:17.545
- [Morwen] Hmm, mm.

57
00:06:20.514 --> 00:06:22.617
(soup sloshing)
(fire crackling)

58
00:06:22.683 --> 00:06:24.051
(Morwen exhales)

59
00:06:24.118 --> 00:06:28.723
(waves crashing)

60
00:06:30.024 --> 00:06:35.096
(Morwen exhales)
(fire crackling)

61
00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.006
(dish clanking)

62
00:06:45.072 --> 00:06:49.677
(utensil clanking)

63
00:06:49.744 --> 00:06:52.513
(dish clanking)

64
00:06:55.082 --> 00:06:57.919
(Morwen exhales)

65
00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:04.091
(crickets chirping)

66
00:07:04.158 --> 00:07:05.559
(brooding music)

67
00:07:05.626 --> 00:07:07.995
- [children] <i>The fox fell out</i>
<i>on a chilly night.</i>

68
00:07:08.062 --> 00:07:11.098
<i>He prayed to the moon</i>
<i>to give him light.</i>

69
00:07:11.165 --> 00:07:14.467
<i>The fox and his wife</i>
<i>without any strife,</i>

70
00:07:14.535 --> 00:07:17.705
<i>cut up the goose with</i>
<i>a fork and knife.</i>

71
00:07:17.772 --> 00:07:20.107
<i>And the little</i>
<i>ones chewed on the bones,</i>

72
00:07:20.174 --> 00:07:22.276
<i>and bones, and bones.</i>

73
00:07:22.343 --> 00:07:23.811
(children laughing)

74
00:07:23.878 --> 00:07:28.382
(tender music)

75
00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:35.222
(waves lapping)

76
00:07:36.023 --> 00:07:37.591
- [child's voice]
Anne, come back.

77
00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:43.331
(dramatic music)

78
00:07:44.231 --> 00:07:47.068
(dramatic music)

79
00:07:48.436 --> 00:07:51.505
(crickets chirping)

80
00:07:54.275 --> 00:07:57.178
(plants rustling)

81
00:07:59.547 --> 00:08:02.750
- [Morwen] You have a way with
this stubborn ground.

82
00:08:02.817 --> 00:08:06.587
Oh, I could never get
anything to grow here.

83
00:08:08.322 --> 00:08:12.259
These beet roots will
be popular at market.

84
00:08:12.326 --> 00:08:13.928
We can barter them

85
00:08:15.396 --> 00:08:18.966
and this.
(chain clinking)

86
00:08:21.135 --> 00:08:22.937
- Will you be selling that one?

87
00:08:23.004 --> 00:08:23.938
- Aye.

88
00:08:25.172 --> 00:08:27.174
And we'll have bread
to eat tonight.

89
00:08:27.241 --> 00:08:30.945
(feet shuffling)
(Morwen exhales)

90
00:08:31.012 --> 00:08:31.946
- Be safe.

91
00:08:34.148 --> 00:08:37.184
- My son chose well
when he picked a wife.

92
00:08:37.251 --> 00:08:38.552
You're my jewel.

93
00:08:38.619 --> 00:08:40.454
(Anne laughs)

94
00:08:40.521 --> 00:08:42.790
I'm always careful.
I know the roads.

95
00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.163
(eerie music)

96
00:08:50.865 --> 00:08:55.970
(leaves rustling)

97
00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:05.413
(Anne humming)

98
00:09:09.917 --> 00:09:10.851
- [Seamus] <i>Anne?</i>

99
00:09:13.154 --> 00:09:15.423
(footsteps plodding)
(soft music)

100
00:09:15.489 --> 00:09:16.724
There you are.

101
00:09:18.659 --> 00:09:20.261
(wistful music)

102
00:09:20.327 --> 00:09:22.229
- Seamus, you're back.

103
00:09:23.964 --> 00:09:25.933
- I'm here, my love.

104
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.935
(Anne laughs)

105
00:09:31.739 --> 00:09:34.575
(brooding music)

106
00:09:38.579 --> 00:09:40.281
(Seamus groaning)

107
00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:47.788
(Seamus screaming)
(brooding music continues)

108
00:09:50.858 --> 00:09:51.759
Help me.

109
00:09:53.528 --> 00:09:55.329
Pain.
(dramatic music)

110
00:09:55.396 --> 00:09:58.899
(Anne gasps and exhales)

111
00:10:06.674 --> 00:10:08.209
(Morwen chuckles)

112
00:10:08.275 --> 00:10:13.380
(pot clanking)

113
00:10:14.381 --> 00:10:15.416
- Is this all?
- Aye.

114
00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:17.151
Except...

115
00:10:22.089 --> 00:10:23.257
- Oh, Morwen.

116
00:10:24.258 --> 00:10:26.561
(kissing)

117
00:10:26.627 --> 00:10:28.696
(vegetable thuds)
(Anne laughs)

118
00:10:28.762 --> 00:10:31.832
(knife rasping and thudding)

119
00:10:31.899 --> 00:10:33.400
(Anne exhales)

120
00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:34.468
(knife thuds)

121
00:10:34.536 --> 00:10:37.004
(grim music)

122
00:10:37.071 --> 00:10:37.972
Oh.

123
00:10:43.644 --> 00:10:44.745
(Morwen exhales)

124
00:10:44.812 --> 00:10:46.380
I...
(vegetable thuds)

125
00:10:46.447 --> 00:10:49.150
- Damn.
(dishes clanking)

126
00:10:53.654 --> 00:10:55.756
No matter. I don't mind.

127
00:10:57.124 --> 00:10:59.093
I've got my sweet Anne.

128
00:11:00.327 --> 00:11:03.297
Be patient. The
Virgin will provide.

129
00:11:04.665 --> 00:11:05.900
The Lady is merciful.

130
00:11:05.966 --> 00:11:07.602
She will to it that we have

131
00:11:07.668 --> 00:11:10.671
what we need to
fill our bellies.

132
00:11:10.738 --> 00:11:13.508
(fire crackling)

133
00:11:13.575 --> 00:11:17.845
- And I pray, too, that
Seamus will return soon.

134
00:11:17.912 --> 00:11:21.382
I thought he would be
here with us again by now.

135
00:11:21.448 --> 00:11:23.384
(Anne sighs)

136
00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.351
(pensive music)

137
00:11:24.418 --> 00:11:25.986
It's been so long.

138
00:11:27.522 --> 00:11:31.058
- He'll have to put an end
to this curse of poverty

139
00:11:31.125 --> 00:11:33.294
and become a wealthy man.

140
00:11:34.629 --> 00:11:38.866
Have faith in his
ambition. (laughs)

141
00:11:38.933 --> 00:11:41.235
This war will make us rich.

142
00:11:43.103 --> 00:11:47.341
- I do.

143
00:11:53.515 --> 00:11:58.553
(waves lapping)
(birds squawking)

144
00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:01.488
(grass rustling)

145
00:12:04.391 --> 00:12:07.662
(man singing faintly)

146
00:12:11.799 --> 00:12:15.302
♪ <i>Aye, aye, this night is long</i> ♪

147
00:12:15.369 --> 00:12:18.939
♪ <i>I most unjustly</i> ♪

148
00:12:19.006 --> 00:12:22.176
♪ <i>Sorrow, and mourn, and fast</i> ♪

149
00:12:22.243 --> 00:12:24.011
(water pattering)
(waves lapping)

150
00:12:24.078 --> 00:12:26.981
♪ <i>Aye, this night is long ♪</i>

151
00:12:27.047 --> 00:12:29.950
♪ <i>I most unjustly</i> ♪
(bag rustling)

152
00:12:30.017 --> 00:12:34.288
(fish thuds)
♪ <i>Sorrow, and mourn, and fast</i> ♪

153
00:12:34.355 --> 00:12:37.124
(man singing faintly)
(pensive music)

154
00:12:37.191 --> 00:12:38.092
- Jago.

155
00:12:39.493 --> 00:12:44.231
(waves lapping)
(pensive music continues)

156
00:12:48.603 --> 00:12:49.870
- Hello, Anne.

157
00:12:51.338 --> 00:12:53.307
- Back from Tewkesbury?

158
00:12:54.174 --> 00:12:55.075
- I am.

159
00:12:57.244 --> 00:12:59.413
- Are the wars over then?

160
00:13:01.882 --> 00:13:06.153
- Over for me.
(waves lapping)

161
00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:09.089
- Then it's good
to see you again.

162
00:13:12.226 --> 00:13:14.295
But where is my husband?

163
00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:19.867
(waves lapping)
(pensive music continues)

164
00:13:19.933 --> 00:13:25.005
(Jago slurping)
(soup sloshing)

165
00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.790
- Where is my son?

166
00:13:45.627 --> 00:13:50.699
(Jago sucking fingers)
(fire crackling)

167
00:13:51.932 --> 00:13:53.500
- Rivers of blood,

168
00:13:54.335 --> 00:13:56.504
(pensive music)

169
00:13:56.571 --> 00:13:57.471
bodies,

170
00:14:01.475 --> 00:14:06.480
his Lord's liberty
and maintenance, they
all look the same,

171
00:14:08.115 --> 00:14:10.417
mangled and dirtied.

172
00:14:10.484 --> 00:14:13.788
(fire crackling)
(pensive music continues)

173
00:14:13.854 --> 00:14:16.791
Seamus and I, we,
we had to leave.

174
00:14:24.833 --> 00:14:26.233
You've known me.

175
00:14:29.269 --> 00:14:31.905
I'm a fisherman, not a soldier.

176
00:14:35.476 --> 00:14:37.846
What army does Richard have?

177
00:14:40.481 --> 00:14:42.316
Armies and fishermen
forced to square

178
00:14:42.383 --> 00:14:46.755
against some unknown man
at the other end of battle,

179
00:14:46.821 --> 00:14:49.557
and one of us'll kill the other,

180
00:14:51.559 --> 00:14:54.061
and it won't change anything.

181
00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:58.232
It won't cease the fighting,

182
00:14:58.298 --> 00:14:59.834
but the crown
would've lost a son

183
00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:02.069
who would've grown her
crops and fed her people

184
00:15:02.136 --> 00:15:05.272
if only she'd give him
a chance to come home.

185
00:15:05.339 --> 00:15:07.575
- You abandoned your post.

186
00:15:08.543 --> 00:15:11.345
(pensive music continues)

187
00:15:11.412 --> 00:15:13.681
- We agreed we would leave

188
00:15:15.884 --> 00:15:19.286
at night while the
captains were asleep.

189
00:15:21.321 --> 00:15:22.389
But we were,

190
00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:27.928
we were beset by thieves.

191
00:15:30.698 --> 00:15:31.866
They beat us,

192
00:15:34.034 --> 00:15:36.103
took what little we had.

193
00:15:41.341 --> 00:15:42.911
They killed Seamus

194
00:15:45.412 --> 00:15:46.313
nigh on.

195
00:15:51.385 --> 00:15:54.556
We should never have
left this place,

196
00:15:55.956 --> 00:16:00.294
this little cove.
(fire crackling)

197
00:16:01.629 --> 00:16:03.798
He was my dearest friend.

198
00:16:06.601 --> 00:16:08.168
- You saw him die?

199
00:16:11.138 --> 00:16:12.072
- Aye.

200
00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:21.014
- (exhales) How,
how did it happen?

201
00:16:21.081 --> 00:16:24.151
- Uh, it's too cruel for
a woman's ears, Morwen.

202
00:16:24.218 --> 00:16:27.087
- Oh, I'm no stranger
to cruelty, pup.

203
00:16:27.154 --> 00:16:29.858
My heart is already hard.

204
00:16:29.924 --> 00:16:31.659
- They split him neck to navel.

205
00:16:31.726 --> 00:16:34.061
(Seamus screaming)
(blood squelching)

206
00:16:34.127 --> 00:16:36.096
(Anne whimpers)

207
00:16:36.163 --> 00:16:41.268
(pensive music)
(fire crackling)

208
00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:51.311
I am sorry.

209
00:16:52.479 --> 00:16:57.552
(fire crackling)
(somber music)

210
00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:02.657
(waves lapping)
(somber music continues)

211
00:17:05.459 --> 00:17:08.128
(Anne sobbing)

212
00:17:10.698 --> 00:17:11.866
- Ah, Seamus.

213
00:17:15.469 --> 00:17:17.037
You were my heart.

214
00:17:21.441 --> 00:17:25.245
My chest is empty. (sobbing)

215
00:17:34.656 --> 00:17:38.726
(birds chirping)
(pensive music)

216
00:17:38.793 --> 00:17:41.596
(grass rustling)

217
00:17:59.146 --> 00:18:02.082
(Jago humming)

218
00:18:02.149 --> 00:18:07.220
(net rustling)
(Jago continues humming)

219
00:18:17.031 --> 00:18:19.867
(brooding music)

220
00:18:24.505 --> 00:18:29.577
(reins clattering)
(brooding music)

221
00:18:31.946 --> 00:18:35.516
(horse nickering)
(hoof thudding)

222
00:18:35.583 --> 00:18:38.753
(voices whispering)

223
00:18:45.225 --> 00:18:50.297
(Anne exhales)
(birds chirping)

224
00:18:51.032 --> 00:18:53.768
(pensive music)

225
00:18:59.373 --> 00:19:01.776
- My son is not coming back,

226
00:19:07.147 --> 00:19:09.249
and you, left childless,

227
00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:17.290
a girl with no husband. (laughs)

228
00:19:19.393 --> 00:19:22.964
He's gone into dirt
with the rest of them.

229
00:19:24.932 --> 00:19:30.004
We're truly alone.
(pensive music continues)

230
00:19:31.572 --> 00:19:34.142
What, (sighs)

231
00:19:36.443 --> 00:19:38.680
what, what will we do now?

232
00:19:42.817 --> 00:19:45.485
(bag rustling)

233
00:19:46.319 --> 00:19:49.891
(Morwen exhales)

234
00:19:49.957 --> 00:19:52.459
I, I wanted to see him again.

235
00:19:57.865 --> 00:20:02.970
(clothes rustling)
(pensive music continues)

236
00:20:06.107 --> 00:20:08.442
(floor creaking)

237
00:20:08.509 --> 00:20:13.581
(grass rustling)
(pensive music continues)

238
00:20:24.391 --> 00:20:27.161
(waves lapping)

239
00:20:40.708 --> 00:20:45.780
(boat creaking)
(waves continue lapping)

240
00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.586
(dramatic music)

241
00:20:51.652 --> 00:20:56.557
(brooding music)

242
00:21:03.497 --> 00:21:06.234
(pensive music)

243
00:21:14.407 --> 00:21:19.479
(knife rasping)
(castaway grunting)

244
00:21:25.285 --> 00:21:30.390
(body thudding)
(birds chirping)

245
00:21:31.759 --> 00:21:33.161
It's safe. Come.

246
00:21:35.797 --> 00:21:40.234
(footsteps plodding)
(pensive music continues)

247
00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:43.137
(coins clinking)

248
00:21:44.806 --> 00:21:45.907
- More dead?

249
00:21:47.809 --> 00:21:50.578
- Yeah, drowned like the others.

250
00:21:53.147 --> 00:21:54.749
(coins clinking)

251
00:21:54.816 --> 00:21:57.552
- Have mercy on those
that crave thy mercy.

252
00:21:57.618 --> 00:21:59.220
Have grace unto them
and make it such

253
00:21:59.287 --> 00:22:02.056
that they may, too,
enjoy thy grace.

254
00:22:02.123 --> 00:22:03.024
Go forward to life.

255
00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:05.392
(bag rustling)

256
00:22:05.458 --> 00:22:09.030
- Wasting your
prayers on the wicked.

257
00:22:09.096 --> 00:22:11.933
God has laid his
judgment on 'em.

258
00:22:13.466 --> 00:22:15.269
(footsteps plodding)

259
00:22:15.335 --> 00:22:16.237
(door clattering)

260
00:22:16.304 --> 00:22:18.072
(feet shuffling)

261
00:22:18.139 --> 00:22:20.575
(hand thuds)

262
00:22:20.641 --> 00:22:22.276
(items clattering)

263
00:22:22.342 --> 00:22:26.113
God is smiling at us
to send such good luck.

264
00:22:29.016 --> 00:22:30.450
(boot rasping)
(pensive music continues)

265
00:22:30.518 --> 00:22:32.854
(boot thuds)

266
00:22:32.920 --> 00:22:37.992
(clothes rustling)
(pensive music continues)

267
00:22:39.760 --> 00:22:42.395
(Anne sighs)

268
00:22:42.462 --> 00:22:47.068
He smashed those pirates against
our rocks for our benefit.

269
00:22:47.134 --> 00:22:48.035
- Yes.

270
00:22:49.469 --> 00:22:52.372
(Morwen grunting)

271
00:22:56.110 --> 00:22:58.411
(body rasping)

272
00:22:58.478 --> 00:23:00.815
- I'll trade these
trinkets in market

273
00:23:00.882 --> 00:23:03.718
and be back before
the sun is set.

274
00:23:03.784 --> 00:23:08.856
(footsteps plodding)
(pensive music continues)

275
00:23:12.159 --> 00:23:13.094
(pot clanking)

276
00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:15.563
(soup burbling)

277
00:23:15.630 --> 00:23:20.701
(soup sloshing)
(fire crackling)

278
00:23:24.171 --> 00:23:27.141
(utensil clanking)

279
00:23:27.208 --> 00:23:30.912
(birds chirping and squawking)

280
00:23:30.978 --> 00:23:36.050
(pensive music continues)
(birds continue squawking)

281
00:23:39.320 --> 00:23:42.523
(horse neighing)

282
00:23:42.590 --> 00:23:45.425
(brooding music)

283
00:23:50.264 --> 00:23:55.369
(feet pattering)
(brooding music continues)

284
00:23:58.438 --> 00:24:01.375
(birds squawking)

285
00:24:04.412 --> 00:24:06.981
- [Anne] I think
there's a man out there.

286
00:24:07.048 --> 00:24:11.118
- Silly child, there's
no one out there, hon.

287
00:24:11.185 --> 00:24:15.488
Sometimes I think you're
a bit mad (laughs)

288
00:24:15.556 --> 00:24:20.628
like your mother before you.
(brooding music continues)

289
00:24:21.595 --> 00:24:23.297
(Morwen exhales)

290
00:24:23.364 --> 00:24:24.999
Go on. Rest, child.

291
00:24:28.869 --> 00:24:31.605
(pensive music)

292
00:24:32.707 --> 00:24:37.511
(birds chirping)
(grass rustling)

293
00:24:38.813 --> 00:24:43.451
(Jago humming)
(footsteps plodding)

294
00:24:57.098 --> 00:24:58.332
- Hello, Anne.

295
00:24:59.467 --> 00:25:03.838
Are you well?
(grass rustling)

296
00:25:03.904 --> 00:25:06.040
Where are you walking to?

297
00:25:07.174 --> 00:25:08.709
- To church.

298
00:25:08.776 --> 00:25:12.580
- Ah, I've lost my taste
for pretty sermons.

299
00:25:12.646 --> 00:25:15.483
(grass rustling)

300
00:25:17.118 --> 00:25:20.821
But don't you know you
shouldn't be walking alone here?

301
00:25:20.888 --> 00:25:22.923
There are bad men on this road.

302
00:25:22.990 --> 00:25:24.291
They would steal a girl like you

303
00:25:24.358 --> 00:25:25.526
away from home.
- I know the path.

304
00:25:25.593 --> 00:25:26.727
I'll be safe.

305
00:25:29.330 --> 00:25:31.599
- I'll walk with you.

306
00:25:31.665 --> 00:25:33.434
Perhaps you'd like the company.

307
00:25:33.501 --> 00:25:37.338
- I shouldn't walk with a
man who's not my husband.

308
00:25:38.539 --> 00:25:40.808
- Your husband's dead.

309
00:25:40.875 --> 00:25:44.812
(pensive music)
(grass rustling)

310
00:25:44.879 --> 00:25:48.015
- Walk well enough
without your help.

311
00:25:50.684 --> 00:25:53.421
(Jago sniffs)
(pensive music continues)

312
00:25:53.487 --> 00:25:58.527
(water sloshing)
(birds chirping)

313
00:26:02.663 --> 00:26:07.735
(item clattering)
(grass rustling)

314
00:26:16.310 --> 00:26:17.711
- Hello, Morwen.

315
00:26:18.879 --> 00:26:21.615
What a fine day.
(grass rustling)

316
00:26:21.682 --> 00:26:25.753
Sun is nearly shining,
and the breeze is gentle.

317
00:26:26.921 --> 00:26:28.322
- Come, Anne.
(brooding music)

318
00:26:28.389 --> 00:26:31.225
(grass rustling)

319
00:26:34.061 --> 00:26:34.962
- Hag.

320
00:26:35.930 --> 00:26:37.865
(knife thudding)

321
00:26:37.932 --> 00:26:43.037
(hands rasping)
(footsteps plodding)

322
00:26:43.704 --> 00:26:45.106
(knife thudding)

323
00:26:45.172 --> 00:26:47.441
- You were at
church all morning?

324
00:26:47.509 --> 00:26:48.909
- [Anne] Mm-hmm.

325
00:26:50.444 --> 00:26:53.814
(food sizzling)
(fire crackling)

326
00:26:53.881 --> 00:26:56.283
- And he followed you there?

327
00:26:57.284 --> 00:26:58.486
- [Anne] Yes.

328
00:26:58.553 --> 00:27:03.592
(Morwen groans)
(fire crackling)

329
00:27:04.559 --> 00:27:05.893
- I never liked that boy.

330
00:27:08.129 --> 00:27:10.164
(Morwen laughs)
(pensive music)

331
00:27:10.231 --> 00:27:12.900
He always had a
jealous look about him,

332
00:27:12.967 --> 00:27:13.834
(knife thudding)

333
00:27:13.901 --> 00:27:15.703
even as a child.

334
00:27:15.769 --> 00:27:20.641
(footsteps plodding)
(pensive music continues)

335
00:27:20.708 --> 00:27:23.512
(birds chirping)

336
00:27:25.412 --> 00:27:29.049
Always following
Seamus everywhere.

337
00:27:29.116 --> 00:27:31.852
I saw the angry look in his eye,

338
00:27:32.887 --> 00:27:34.121
parentless rat.

339
00:27:35.489 --> 00:27:37.858
(birds chirping)
(pensive music continues)

340
00:27:37.925 --> 00:27:41.162
(laughs) Look like a stray dog,

341
00:27:41.228 --> 00:27:44.365
always sniffing
around for scraps.

342
00:27:44.431 --> 00:27:48.903
(rain pattering)
(pensive music continues)

343
00:27:48.969 --> 00:27:52.373
(footsteps plodding)

344
00:27:52.439 --> 00:27:55.943
Greed, has Jago's heart,
I'm sure of
it.

345
00:27:58.679 --> 00:28:01.949
- It's...
(knife thudding)

346
00:28:02.016 --> 00:28:05.452
We were such close friends
before I married Seamus.

347
00:28:05.520 --> 00:28:08.889
I, I had forgotten
our time together.

348
00:28:08.956 --> 00:28:11.859
I, I do not think
him an evil man.

349
00:28:13.460 --> 00:28:18.399
- (laughs) Evil is
not always obvious.

350
00:28:18.465 --> 00:28:21.735
(fire crackling)
(pensive music)

351
00:28:21.802 --> 00:28:23.704
This is a time of war.

352
00:28:26.140 --> 00:28:29.710
There is a lot that
spreads all around us.

353
00:28:31.178 --> 00:28:34.248
Demons walk the earth
in the shape of men.

354
00:28:36.217 --> 00:28:39.220
(hooves clopping)
(metal clanging)

355
00:28:39.286 --> 00:28:43.390
Stay with me, and you'll
have nothing to fear.

356
00:28:43.457 --> 00:28:46.193
With me, you'll never be cursed.

357
00:28:47.061 --> 00:28:48.896
But if you disobey me,

358
00:28:51.899 --> 00:28:56.605
the knights of hell will
drag you down into the pit,

359
00:28:56.671 --> 00:29:00.107
and there'll be nothing
I can do to save you.

360
00:29:00.174 --> 00:29:05.212
(hooves clopping)
(horse neighing)

361
00:29:05.879 --> 00:29:06.780
- I, I promise.

362
00:29:06.847 --> 00:29:07.748
- Oh, oh.

363
00:29:11.418 --> 00:29:14.255
(fire crackling)

364
00:29:15.523 --> 00:29:19.927
(birds chirping)
(footsteps plodding)

365
00:29:19.994 --> 00:29:23.531
(person speaking faintly)

366
00:29:25.866 --> 00:29:29.203
(footsteps plodding)

367
00:29:29.270 --> 00:29:30.705
(door creaking)

368
00:29:30.771 --> 00:29:32.206
Ah, Anne, come.

369
00:29:33.907 --> 00:29:35.476
(door clattering)

370
00:29:35.543 --> 00:29:38.647
Friar Penros has found
us on the road home.

371
00:29:38.713 --> 00:29:41.282
- Friar Penros.
- Hello, Anne.

372
00:29:43.183 --> 00:29:46.987
- Sorry we don't have
more to offer you.

373
00:29:47.054 --> 00:29:49.724
This is the last of our stores.

374
00:29:50.759 --> 00:29:52.893
These are difficult times.

375
00:29:52.960 --> 00:29:57.131
- Course, uh, but do you
have anything to drink?

376
00:29:57.197 --> 00:29:58.999
My throat is parched.

377
00:30:01.135 --> 00:30:02.069
Hmm.

378
00:30:02.803 --> 00:30:04.471
(cup thuds)

379
00:30:04.539 --> 00:30:07.776
(Friar Penros laughs)

380
00:30:08.576 --> 00:30:11.478
(liquid sloshing)

381
00:30:13.447 --> 00:30:14.348
Bless you.

382
00:30:15.215 --> 00:30:18.152
(footsteps plodding)

383
00:30:18.218 --> 00:30:19.119
Mm.

384
00:30:20.755 --> 00:30:23.490
(lips smacking)

385
00:30:25.059 --> 00:30:26.060
(water sloshing)

386
00:30:26.126 --> 00:30:27.861
(cup thuds)
Mm.

387
00:30:27.928 --> 00:30:30.765
(fire crackling)

388
00:30:34.569 --> 00:30:36.970
Forgive me, Lord, my hunger.

389
00:30:39.574 --> 00:30:41.375
Blessed us, oh, Lord,
and these, thy gifts,

390
00:30:41.442 --> 00:30:43.611
which we are about to receive

391
00:30:43.678 --> 00:30:47.549
from thy bounty through
Christ our Lord, amen.

392
00:30:47.615 --> 00:30:48.916
- Amen.
- Amen.

393
00:30:48.982 --> 00:30:51.753
- Mm, brings joy to my heart

394
00:30:51.820 --> 00:30:55.690
to see two such pious women.
(pensive music)

395
00:30:55.757 --> 00:30:57.191
(cup thuds)
(lips smacking)

396
00:30:57.257 --> 00:30:59.594
I'll show you a
special relic,

397
00:30:59.661 --> 00:31:02.963
so you can share in the
glory of my pilgrimage.

398
00:31:03.030 --> 00:31:08.135
(box and items clattering)
(pensive music continues)

399
00:31:15.309 --> 00:31:16.410
Just put that back.

400
00:31:16.477 --> 00:31:17.478
(bottle thuds)

401
00:31:17.545 --> 00:31:18.646
Here we are.

402
00:31:20.715 --> 00:31:25.820
- Oh, how beautiful.
(pensive music continues)

403
00:31:26.453 --> 00:31:27.321
- Open it.

404
00:31:29.456 --> 00:31:32.159
(lid clanks)

405
00:31:32.226 --> 00:31:33.327
- [Anne] Oh.

406
00:31:33.394 --> 00:31:35.764
- Do not touch, child. Careful.

407
00:31:35.830 --> 00:31:39.233
These trinkets are more
valuable than you can imagine.

408
00:31:39.299 --> 00:31:42.936
- [Anne] (laughs) It's
wonderful, Father.

409
00:31:43.003 --> 00:31:46.407
- For our Lord
Jesus's blessed life

410
00:31:46.473 --> 00:31:48.375
from a Bethlehem dove.

411
00:31:50.812 --> 00:31:52.714
Three silver pieces,

412
00:31:54.148 --> 00:31:57.619
special price for
such a faithful flock.

413
00:31:57.685 --> 00:31:59.754
- We can't afford
such beautiful gifts.

414
00:31:59.821 --> 00:32:00.855
We don't have any money.

415
00:32:00.954 --> 00:32:03.357
(lid thuds)

416
00:32:05.593 --> 00:32:06.661
- Very well then.

417
00:32:06.728 --> 00:32:08.295
(box clattering)

418
00:32:08.362 --> 00:32:10.030
(footsteps plodding)
(lips smacking)

419
00:32:10.097 --> 00:32:14.334
- Who else knows you've
returned from your travels?

420
00:32:14.401 --> 00:32:17.371
- You are but the first.
(utensil clanking)

421
00:32:17.438 --> 00:32:21.275
- I'm sure you're eager
to continue your journey.

422
00:32:21.341 --> 00:32:25.647
- Aye, I'm just passing
through. I am London bound.

423
00:32:27.549 --> 00:32:29.950
Well, thank you for
your hospitality.

424
00:32:30.017 --> 00:32:31.485
I must continue my journey

425
00:32:31.553 --> 00:32:32.854
before too much of
the day has passed.

426
00:32:32.921 --> 00:32:37.926
(items clattering)
(pensive music)

427
00:32:39.226 --> 00:32:41.061
A blessing before I go.

428
00:32:41.128 --> 00:32:45.299
(Friar Penros
inhales and exhales)

429
00:32:45.365 --> 00:32:48.368
The Lord shall preserve
thee from all evil.

430
00:32:48.435 --> 00:32:52.172
Yea, it is even he that
shall keep thy soul.

431
00:32:52.239 --> 00:32:55.510
Glory to the Father as
it was in the beginning.

432
00:32:55.577 --> 00:33:00.648
Lord have mercy upon us, our
Father, which art in heaven,

433
00:33:02.049 --> 00:33:03.918
and lead us not into
temptation, amen.

434
00:33:05.285 --> 00:33:08.422
- Amen.
(pensive music)

435
00:33:08.489 --> 00:33:12.092
- Beware of heretical
thoughts, my friend.

436
00:33:12.159 --> 00:33:13.895
Those lies do nothing for you

437
00:33:13.962 --> 00:33:18.098
but illuminate the hideous
truths that surround us.

438
00:33:18.165 --> 00:33:20.768
Stay in the warm, blind bliss.

439
00:33:22.069 --> 00:33:22.904
(dramatic music)
(Friar Penros grunts)

440
00:33:22.971 --> 00:33:24.104
(knife rasping)

441
00:33:24.171 --> 00:33:25.038
(Friar Penros screams)

442
00:33:25.105 --> 00:33:26.006
- No, no.

443
00:33:27.775 --> 00:33:29.109
(Friar Penros grunts)
(knife rasping)

444
00:33:29.176 --> 00:33:30.177
(Morwen screams)
No.

445
00:33:30.244 --> 00:33:31.378
(body thudding)

446
00:33:31.445 --> 00:33:32.947
(Friar Penros coughing)

447
00:33:33.013 --> 00:33:34.281
- [Morwen] Move aside.

448
00:33:34.348 --> 00:33:35.215
(Anne whimpering)

449
00:33:35.315 --> 00:33:37.417
(body rasping)

450
00:33:37.484 --> 00:33:38.753
(Anne gasps)

451
00:33:38.820 --> 00:33:42.724
(Anne whimpering and panting)

452
00:33:47.595 --> 00:33:49.429
- What did you do?

453
00:33:49.496 --> 00:33:51.799
- He was making a mess.

454
00:33:51.866 --> 00:33:55.235
- Are, are you mad? He's,
he's a, he's a man of God.

455
00:33:55.302 --> 00:33:56.704
He's a holy man.

456
00:33:57.705 --> 00:34:00.340
- Ah, he wasn't a, a man of God.

457
00:34:02.610 --> 00:34:05.479
He was a charlatan and a fool.

458
00:34:05.547 --> 00:34:07.715
He was a false pretender.

459
00:34:09.216 --> 00:34:12.720
These items will feed
us through the winter.

460
00:34:13.688 --> 00:34:16.290
(Anne sobbing)

461
00:34:16.356 --> 00:34:17.692
You understand.

462
00:34:19.226 --> 00:34:22.897
You, you understand.
(pensive music)

463
00:34:22.964 --> 00:34:24.766
(Anne breathing heavily)

464
00:34:24.832 --> 00:34:27.669
(brooding music)

465
00:34:30.038 --> 00:34:33.708
(Anne and Morwen grunting)

466
00:34:39.479 --> 00:34:42.149
(thunder rumbling)

467
00:34:42.215 --> 00:34:44.919
(both grunting)
(body thudding)

468
00:34:44.986 --> 00:34:45.887
Come on.

469
00:34:46.721 --> 00:34:49.591
(Morwen grunting)

470
00:34:53.360 --> 00:34:58.432
(water sloshing)
(brooding music continues)

471
00:35:00.334 --> 00:35:05.405
(cloth rasping)
(brooding music continues)

472
00:35:08.108 --> 00:35:10.945
(grass rustling)

473
00:35:12.346 --> 00:35:16.951
(water sloshing)
(brooding music continues)

474
00:35:17.619 --> 00:35:20.287
(cloth rasping)

475
00:35:26.527 --> 00:35:31.599
(thunder rumbling)
(brooding music continues)

476
00:35:36.203 --> 00:35:39.707
There was talk around
Friar Penros, you know,

477
00:35:39.774 --> 00:35:42.476
that he was a philander.

478
00:35:42.543 --> 00:35:46.914
His heart had been claimed by
Mammon, by the lusty feels

479
00:35:46.981 --> 00:35:50.685
for material wealth,
and shiny objects,

480
00:35:50.752 --> 00:35:54.254
and the soft gaze of
foolish young girls.

481
00:35:55.790 --> 00:35:57.190
He was false.

482
00:36:03.131 --> 00:36:04.032
- Morwen.

483
00:36:06.634 --> 00:36:07.535
- Yes.

484
00:36:10.838 --> 00:36:14.942
- I don't know if I can
be as strong as you, as,

485
00:36:18.311 --> 00:36:19.379
as ruthless.

486
00:36:23.918 --> 00:36:27.320
I do not know if we
did the right thing.

487
00:36:28.723 --> 00:36:31.693
- All that matters
is that we survive.

488
00:36:33.828 --> 00:36:35.997
You must be very cautious

489
00:36:37.799 --> 00:36:39.701
not to give in to sin,

490
00:36:41.268 --> 00:36:42.170
to lust.

491
00:36:46.206 --> 00:36:49.877
I couldn't bear the
thought of you in hell,

492
00:36:51.679 --> 00:36:54.716
never to be reunited
with my son,

493
00:36:54.782 --> 00:36:58.753
your sweet husband in
Heaven where he sits now.

494
00:37:01.689 --> 00:37:03.725
You must be vigilant.

495
00:37:03.791 --> 00:37:05.358
You must be pious.

496
00:37:06.627 --> 00:37:09.063
You will be reunited with him.

497
00:37:09.130 --> 00:37:11.264
Isn't that what you want?

498
00:37:12.567 --> 00:37:16.504
- Of course.
(fire crackling)

499
00:37:18.906 --> 00:37:21.843
(Morwen laughs)

500
00:37:21.909 --> 00:37:25.613
- Well, mm.
(pensive music)

501
00:37:27.380 --> 00:37:29.382
Mm, you're a good girl.

502
00:37:34.722 --> 00:37:39.794
(birds chirping)
(pensive music continues)

503
00:37:43.598 --> 00:37:46.100
(rug thuds)

504
00:37:46.167 --> 00:37:51.205
(metal rasping)
(pensive music continues)

505
00:37:58.246 --> 00:37:59.647
- [Anne] Morwen.

506
00:38:01.348 --> 00:38:02.482
(birds chirping)

507
00:38:02.550 --> 00:38:05.620
(animal squealing)

508
00:38:10.558 --> 00:38:12.425
(birds chirping)
(brooding music)

509
00:38:27.642 --> 00:38:32.747
(birds chirping)
(brooding music continues)

510
00:38:37.785 --> 00:38:38.719
(animal screeching)

511
00:38:38.786 --> 00:38:40.922
(footsteps plodding)

512
00:38:40.988 --> 00:38:46.093
(birds squawking)
(footsteps continue plodding)

513
00:38:47.261 --> 00:38:52.300
(bag rustling)
(pensive music)

514
00:39:00.308 --> 00:39:03.144
(grass rustling)

515
00:39:05.112 --> 00:39:09.784
(dramatic music)
(horses neighing)

516
00:39:09.851 --> 00:39:12.787
(hooves clopping)

517
00:39:16.791 --> 00:39:18.391
(sword rasping)
(Anne screaming)

518
00:39:18.458 --> 00:39:23.363
(hooves clopping)

519
00:39:32.874 --> 00:39:35.475
(Anne gasping)
(voices whispering)

520
00:39:35.543 --> 00:39:36.409
(Anne grunts)

521
00:39:36.476 --> 00:39:39.146
(Anne gasping)

522
00:39:39.213 --> 00:39:42.083
- [Jago] Anne.
(feet pattering)

523
00:39:42.149 --> 00:39:43.450
- Jago.
- Hey.

524
00:39:43.517 --> 00:39:44.652
- Did you see him?
- Did I see who?

525
00:39:44.719 --> 00:39:45.920
- I, I, I think he is a demon.

526
00:39:45.987 --> 00:39:47.221
He's, he's not

527
00:39:47.288 --> 00:39:48.656
from this world.
- Ah, there's-

528
00:39:48.723 --> 00:39:49.657
- He's following me.
- no one there.

529
00:39:49.724 --> 00:39:51.292
There's no one there.

530
00:39:51.359 --> 00:39:52.459
It, it's just us here.
- No, he was there.

531
00:39:52.526 --> 00:39:53.995
He, he wears a, a suit of armor,

532
00:39:54.061 --> 00:39:55.630
and he, he rides a white horse.

533
00:39:55.696 --> 00:39:58.666
- Why would a
demon need a horse?

534
00:39:58.733 --> 00:40:02.503
It's just some soldier traveling
through to Manor Trematon,

535
00:40:02.570 --> 00:40:05.239
someone made of flesh and blood.

536
00:40:05.306 --> 00:40:07.275
Come. Sit down.

537
00:40:07.341 --> 00:40:10.845
(Anne breathing heavily)

538
00:40:21.689 --> 00:40:22.757
Anne.
- Yeah.

539
00:40:26.560 --> 00:40:27.895
- You found me.

540
00:40:32.366 --> 00:40:33.267
- What?

541
00:40:34.735 --> 00:40:38.272
- You were scared, and
you came to find me.

542
00:40:40.007 --> 00:40:41.575
I'm glad you came.

543
00:40:44.078 --> 00:40:45.079
What is it?

544
00:40:47.181 --> 00:40:48.316
- I'm afraid.

545
00:40:49.216 --> 00:40:51.052
(Jago laughs)

546
00:40:51.118 --> 00:40:52.687
- Afraid.

547
00:40:52.753 --> 00:40:56.557
- Don't mock me, afraid
of what might happen.

548
00:40:58.092 --> 00:40:59.860
I don't want to be marked
by a knight of hell.

549
00:40:59.927 --> 00:41:03.463
I don't want to be cursed
and dragged into the pit.

550
00:41:03.531 --> 00:41:06.334
- Cursed, Anne? Are you a child?

551
00:41:06.400 --> 00:41:09.804
- Morwen told me that-
- Ah, that hag.

552
00:41:09.870 --> 00:41:12.173
Doesn't know anything,

553
00:41:12.239 --> 00:41:14.408
just trying to scare you.

554
00:41:16.143 --> 00:41:17.477
- Hell is real.

555
00:41:18.312 --> 00:41:19.246
- Aye.

556
00:41:20.414 --> 00:41:21.749
I've seen hell.

557
00:41:23.317 --> 00:41:27.822
It's 50 leagues in that
direction, and it is real.

558
00:41:27.888 --> 00:41:29.690
(pensive music)

559
00:41:29.757 --> 00:41:33.694
Hell is the war between the
rich men and spilt blood.

560
00:41:34.929 --> 00:41:37.832
But this, Anne,
this is also real.

561
00:41:42.336 --> 00:41:45.272
I want you, Anne,
and you want me.

562
00:41:47.608 --> 00:41:49.276
Come to me tonight.

563
00:41:49.343 --> 00:41:52.079
There'll be no
demons to haunt you.

564
00:41:52.146 --> 00:41:57.151
Meet me where we used to play
as children. Do you remember?

565
00:41:58.419 --> 00:41:59.887
It's just us now.

566
00:42:01.455 --> 00:42:06.494
Come to me tonight.
(pensive music continues)

567
00:42:11.132 --> 00:42:16.203
(grass rustling)

568
00:42:20.608 --> 00:42:24.278
(person humming)
(grass continues rustling)

569
00:42:24.345 --> 00:42:27.181
(brooding music)

570
00:42:29.450 --> 00:42:34.523
(flesh squelching)
(brooding music continues)

571
00:42:49.136 --> 00:42:50.771
- This is my dream.

572
00:42:52.039 --> 00:42:53.974
Go.
(dramatic music)

573
00:42:54.041 --> 00:42:57.111
(crickets chirping)

574
00:42:59.814 --> 00:43:02.616
(bed creaking)

575
00:43:13.861 --> 00:43:15.262
- Are you awake?

576
00:43:19.033 --> 00:43:24.105
(clothes rustling)
(crickets continue chirping)

577
00:43:25.507 --> 00:43:26.508
(floor creaking)

578
00:43:26.575 --> 00:43:29.376
(feet shuffling)

579
00:43:30.579 --> 00:43:33.314
(door creaking)

580
00:43:34.915 --> 00:43:37.118
(door clattering)

581
00:43:37.184 --> 00:43:38.652
(Morwen inhales)

582
00:43:38.719 --> 00:43:42.056
(bedding rustling)
(footsteps plodding)

583
00:43:51.298 --> 00:43:56.403
(animal bellowing)
(eerie music)

584
00:44:14.955 --> 00:44:20.027
(knife rasping)
(fire crackling)

585
00:44:25.567 --> 00:44:27.569
- You came.
(pensive music)

586
00:44:27.636 --> 00:44:29.303
- I shouldn't have.

587
00:44:31.438 --> 00:44:33.174
I shouldn't be here.

588
00:44:39.514 --> 00:44:43.117
(pensive music continues)

589
00:44:57.632 --> 00:45:00.935
(birds chirping)
(waves lapping)

590
00:45:01.001 --> 00:45:03.605
Wake up. (laughs)

591
00:45:03.672 --> 00:45:05.239
I have to go back.

592
00:45:07.007 --> 00:45:09.076
- Come and live with me.

593
00:45:15.382 --> 00:45:17.451
Come live with me.
- I can't.

594
00:45:17.519 --> 00:45:20.522
- Why can't you?
(pensive music continues)

595
00:45:22.189 --> 00:45:23.525
- She needs me.

596
00:45:26.360 --> 00:45:29.263
- That woman can
fend for herself.

597
00:45:33.067 --> 00:45:34.735
- She frightens me.

598
00:45:37.238 --> 00:45:40.007
(leaves rustling)
(pensive music continues)

599
00:45:40.074 --> 00:45:44.579
- [Jago] She will drain
every bit of life out of you.

600
00:45:46.247 --> 00:45:48.516
I can see it clear as day.

601
00:45:52.753 --> 00:45:56.591
Come live with me, and
I will make you happy.

602
00:46:00.327 --> 00:46:03.364
(footsteps plodding)

603
00:46:03.430 --> 00:46:06.534
(voices whispering)

604
00:46:17.444 --> 00:46:19.913
(clothes rustling)

605
00:46:24.885 --> 00:46:27.888
(bedding rustling)

606
00:46:40.267 --> 00:46:41.969
- Where have you been?

607
00:46:42.036 --> 00:46:44.506
(pensive music)

608
00:46:44.572 --> 00:46:46.807
- I wanted some fresh air.

609
00:46:52.946 --> 00:46:55.617
- You know I'd die without you.

610
00:46:59.654 --> 00:47:01.656
I think you're my angel

611
00:47:08.228 --> 00:47:11.633
sent to care for me
in my son's absence.

612
00:47:15.469 --> 00:47:18.305
We're more precious
to each other

613
00:47:19.641 --> 00:47:22.209
than all the treasures
in the world.

614
00:47:24.813 --> 00:47:26.980
I don't want to be alone.

615
00:47:31.519 --> 00:47:32.453
- I know.

616
00:47:36.223 --> 00:47:38.192
(Morwen inhales)

617
00:47:38.258 --> 00:47:40.729
- Know I'll take care of you.

618
00:47:42.463 --> 00:47:46.233
(pensive music continues)

619
00:47:46.300 --> 00:47:48.335
(waves lapping)
(birds chirping)

620
00:48:04.985 --> 00:48:07.054
(pensive music)
(cart clattering)

621
00:48:23.303 --> 00:48:25.272
(cart creaking)
(pensive music continues)

622
00:48:25.339 --> 00:48:27.408
(footsteps plodding)
(crickets chirping)

623
00:48:32.079 --> 00:48:35.449
- What are you doing here
in the middle of the cold?

624
00:48:35.517 --> 00:48:36.818
(footsteps plodding)

625
00:48:36.885 --> 00:48:38.185
(traveler grunts)
(dramatic music)

626
00:48:38.252 --> 00:48:39.920
(knife rasping)
(blood squelching)

627
00:48:39.987 --> 00:48:41.121
- Help me. What are you
doing just standing there?

628
00:48:41.188 --> 00:48:42.657
Help me.
(traveler gagging)

629
00:48:42.724 --> 00:48:46.193
(footsteps plodding)
(both grunting)

630
00:48:46.260 --> 00:48:48.962
Okay. (panting)

631
00:48:49.029 --> 00:48:52.032
He may have valuables
in his pocket. Look.

632
00:48:52.099 --> 00:48:54.101
(footsteps plodding)

633
00:48:54.168 --> 00:48:57.605
(Morwen exhales)
(footsteps continue plodding)

634
00:49:02.777 --> 00:49:04.978
(bag rustling)

635
00:49:05.045 --> 00:49:07.114
(items clattering)
(pensive music continues)

636
00:49:19.761 --> 00:49:22.262
(footsteps plodding)
(pensive music continues)

637
00:49:23.798 --> 00:49:24.899
What's this?

638
00:49:30.070 --> 00:49:32.841
Nothing, it's just
a child's joy.

639
00:49:36.778 --> 00:49:38.445
(bag rustling)

640
00:49:45.986 --> 00:49:47.522
(coins clinking)
(pensive music continues)

641
00:49:47.589 --> 00:49:49.122
(bell tolling)
(coins continue clinking)

642
00:49:59.734 --> 00:50:02.369
(eerie music)

643
00:50:06.674 --> 00:50:08.576
(cloth rasping)

644
00:50:08.643 --> 00:50:11.713
(voices whispering)

645
00:50:16.784 --> 00:50:18.118
(knight exhales)

646
00:50:18.185 --> 00:50:19.854
(dramatic music)
(sword thuds)

647
00:50:19.921 --> 00:50:23.156
(voices whispering)
(knight breathing heavily)

648
00:50:24.091 --> 00:50:27.494
(nuns singing in Latin)

649
00:50:42.010 --> 00:50:47.080
(baby vocalizing)
(pensive music)

650
00:50:54.022 --> 00:50:57.559
(baby crying)
(pensive music continues)

651
00:50:58.292 --> 00:51:03.363
(nuns singing in Latin)
(baby continues crying)

652
00:51:12.040 --> 00:51:12.907
(door clattering)

653
00:51:12.974 --> 00:51:14.943
♪ <i>Amen</i> ♪

654
00:51:16.511 --> 00:51:18.546
(clothes rustling)
(pensive music continues)

655
00:51:29.591 --> 00:51:32.527
- [Priest] God
protect you, child.

656
00:51:35.597 --> 00:51:36.764
(footsteps plodding)
(pensive music continues)

657
00:51:36.831 --> 00:51:39.734
(baby vocalizing)

658
00:51:46.507 --> 00:51:47.976
- Huh, beautiful.

659
00:51:51.579 --> 00:51:52.479
Yeah.

660
00:51:54.414 --> 00:51:55.315
- Morwen.

661
00:51:59.286 --> 00:52:03.323
(baby vocalizing)
(pensive music continues)

662
00:52:03.390 --> 00:52:06.460
(footsteps plodding)

663
00:52:07.795 --> 00:52:10.297
(May laughs)

664
00:52:12.466 --> 00:52:13.400
A gift.

665
00:52:13.467 --> 00:52:16.604
(footsteps plodding)

666
00:52:19.306 --> 00:52:20.975
(item clattering)

667
00:52:21.042 --> 00:52:21.909
(hand knocking)

668
00:52:21.976 --> 00:52:23.111
- [Jago] Anne.

669
00:52:25.113 --> 00:52:27.048
- Stay here, child.

670
00:52:27.115 --> 00:52:29.449
- [Jago] Anne, are ya in there?

671
00:52:29.817 --> 00:52:32.553
(door clattering and creaking)

672
00:52:32.620 --> 00:52:35.023
- [Morwen] What do you want?

673
00:52:36.423 --> 00:52:39.060
(door creaking and clattering)

674
00:52:39.127 --> 00:52:41.428
- What, you're deaf now, too?

675
00:52:41.495 --> 00:52:43.397
It's not you I
want, is it? Anne.

676
00:52:43.463 --> 00:52:45.399
- She came back to me, pup.

677
00:52:45.465 --> 00:52:48.536
Find yourself another
bitch to fuck.

678
00:52:50.170 --> 00:52:52.707
- Ah, move, you sorry
woman, or I'll push through.

679
00:52:52.774 --> 00:52:54.441
(hand thuds)

680
00:52:54.509 --> 00:52:57.145
- Go away.
(pensive music)

681
00:52:59.847 --> 00:53:03.551
- She's young, and strong,
and she can bear a child,

682
00:53:03.618 --> 00:53:05.185
and you would take
that from her?

683
00:53:05.252 --> 00:53:09.557
- (laughs) Yes,
1,000 times, yes.

684
00:53:09.624 --> 00:53:13.127
What joy has a husband or
child ever brought to me?

685
00:53:13.193 --> 00:53:14.696
None,
(saliva sputtering)

686
00:53:14.762 --> 00:53:17.031
only the grief of
losing them too soon

687
00:53:17.098 --> 00:53:20.935
and suffering a long and
angry life after they've gone.

688
00:53:21.002 --> 00:53:23.303
Yes, I would take that from her.

689
00:53:23.370 --> 00:53:26.306
Yes, I would live
through this winter.

690
00:53:26.373 --> 00:53:31.079
Yes, (laughs) I would deny
you the pleasure of her body.

691
00:53:31.145 --> 00:53:34.448
- Ah, to hell with you. (groans)

692
00:53:34.515 --> 00:53:37.350
- And I will take you
straight to hell, fool.

693
00:53:40.888 --> 00:53:44.559
(footsteps plodding)
(pensive music continues)

694
00:53:46.894 --> 00:53:49.163
- Anne, I'll wait for you.

695
00:53:50.798 --> 00:53:52.867
I'll wait for you, Anne.

696
00:53:54.702 --> 00:53:59.239
(Jago spitting)
(pensive music continues)

697
00:54:01.843 --> 00:54:04.512
(door creaking and clattering)

698
00:54:09.150 --> 00:54:11.953
(fire crackling)

699
00:54:15.489 --> 00:54:17.357
- You're upset.

700
00:54:17.424 --> 00:54:21.062
Oh, sweet child, sweet
child, you're upset.

701
00:54:22.864 --> 00:54:23.765
(Anne exhales)

702
00:54:23.831 --> 00:54:25.199
This is our fate.

703
00:54:26.834 --> 00:54:29.003
It is not your destiny. (laughs)

704
00:54:29.070 --> 00:54:31.139
This is where we belong.

705
00:54:34.509 --> 00:54:36.409
You are my son's wife.

706
00:54:38.079 --> 00:54:39.580
I am your family.

707
00:54:42.083 --> 00:54:44.652
I am your responsibility.

708
00:54:44.719 --> 00:54:46.120
It is God's law.

709
00:54:51.626 --> 00:54:56.197
(Morwen sniffing)
(wind howling)

710
00:54:56.264 --> 00:54:58.833
(fire crackling)
(pensive music)

711
00:54:58.900 --> 00:55:01.569
(Anne sobbing)

712
00:55:02.603 --> 00:55:04.939
- Mother, my heart is torn,

713
00:55:08.308 --> 00:55:10.745
and I am hungry all the time

714
00:55:13.147 --> 00:55:15.583
for things that I have lost.

715
00:55:17.317 --> 00:55:20.588
Why would you leave
me here to starve?

716
00:55:23.991 --> 00:55:27.595
(pensive music continues)

717
00:55:29.831 --> 00:55:30.832
Forgive me.

718
00:55:32.967 --> 00:55:35.036
I have an unruly tongue.

719
00:55:37.071 --> 00:55:40.141
Lord God, I am your
servant, always.

720
00:55:44.477 --> 00:55:45.813
But I'm afraid.

721
00:55:51.118 --> 00:55:53.855
What were you trying to tell me?

722
00:55:55.690 --> 00:55:58.358
(pensive music continues)

723
00:56:00.261 --> 00:56:02.730
(Anne sighs)

724
00:56:03.631 --> 00:56:06.534
(leaves rustling)

725
00:56:10.605 --> 00:56:12.405
(pestle thudding)

726
00:56:12.472 --> 00:56:15.943
(pestle rasping and clanking)

727
00:56:16.010 --> 00:56:19.213
(water sloshing)

728
00:56:19.280 --> 00:56:20.915
(kettle thuds)

729
00:56:31.325 --> 00:56:33.227
Morwen, are you awake?

730
00:56:39.800 --> 00:56:42.603
(Morwen snoring)

731
00:56:43.638 --> 00:56:46.240
(fire crackling)

732
00:56:46.307 --> 00:56:48.509
(door creaking and clattering)

733
00:56:51.712 --> 00:56:54.615
(waves lapping)
(pensive music continues)

734
00:56:58.252 --> 00:57:00.321
(birds chirping)

735
00:57:00.388 --> 00:57:01.956
- I heard of a man

736
00:57:03.758 --> 00:57:07.929
who saw a beautiful woman
walking to church every day.

737
00:57:07.995 --> 00:57:12.432
(water sloshing)
(gentle music)

738
00:57:12.499 --> 00:57:15.136
Nobody knew where she was from,

739
00:57:16.938 --> 00:57:19.874
but the man fell
in love with her.

740
00:57:21.575 --> 00:57:25.746
Matha E. Chawalla was his
name, and he loved to sing.

741
00:57:28.082 --> 00:57:30.985
Finally, one day,
he followed her,

742
00:57:34.288 --> 00:57:37.725
and he sang a song
to her as she walked,

743
00:57:41.929 --> 00:57:44.632
and he was never seen again.

744
00:57:44.699 --> 00:57:47.835
(birds chirping and squawking)

745
00:57:47.902 --> 00:57:49.904
- What happened to him?

746
00:57:54.942 --> 00:57:58.145
- Well, I think he
followed her into the sea.

747
00:58:00.614 --> 00:58:02.616
- So she was a mermaid.

748
00:58:04.484 --> 00:58:07.088
(Jago laughs)

749
00:58:08.488 --> 00:58:11.592
Maybe I'll drag you
down into the water.

750
00:58:11.659 --> 00:58:15.963
(Anne laughs)
(gentle music continues)

751
00:58:54.835 --> 00:58:58.906
(chair clattering)
(fire crackling)

752
00:59:00.441 --> 00:59:01.308
- Anne?

753
00:59:03.210 --> 00:59:04.879
(Morwen sighs)

754
00:59:14.488 --> 00:59:16.824
(door clattering)

755
00:59:19.393 --> 00:59:21.929
(feet shuffling)

756
00:59:22.797 --> 00:59:24.698
(Morwen sighs)
(hands rasping)

757
00:59:27.735 --> 00:59:30.237
(footsteps plodding)
(wind rustling)

758
00:59:32.306 --> 00:59:33.207
Anne?

759
00:59:34.975 --> 00:59:37.044
(footsteps plodding)
(wind rustling)

760
00:59:41.382 --> 00:59:43.150
Anne.
(footsteps continue plodding)

761
00:59:43.217 --> 00:59:45.286
(pensive music)
(footsteps continue plodding)

762
00:59:49.256 --> 00:59:50.758
Are you out here?

763
00:59:52.226 --> 00:59:54.962
(horse neighing)
(brooding music)

764
00:59:55.029 --> 00:59:56.597
(hooves clopping)
(brooding music continues)

765
00:59:59.667 --> 01:00:02.470
(feet pattering)

766
01:00:06.407 --> 01:00:08.476
(horse nickering)
(brooding music continues)

767
01:00:12.913 --> 01:00:14.815
(birds squawking)

768
01:00:19.620 --> 01:00:22.022
(hooves clopping)
(brooding music continues)

769
01:00:22.089 --> 01:00:24.593
(metal clanging)
(hooves continue clopping)

770
01:00:43.811 --> 01:00:46.914
(metal rasping)
(brooding music)

771
01:00:52.253 --> 01:00:54.088
(knight exhales)

772
01:00:57.825 --> 01:00:59.528
(Morwen breathing heavily)

773
01:01:01.596 --> 01:01:04.298
Anne.
(pensive music)

774
01:01:10.838 --> 01:01:14.141
(hooves clopping)
(pensive music continues)

775
01:01:30.958 --> 01:01:32.760
(footsteps plodding)

776
01:01:32.826 --> 01:01:35.162
(birds squawking)
(footsteps continue plodding)

777
01:01:37.198 --> 01:01:39.300
(dramatic music)
(metal clanging)

778
01:01:52.813 --> 01:01:55.650
(brooding music)

779
01:01:59.853 --> 01:02:01.989
(footsteps plodding)

780
01:02:05.459 --> 01:02:06.727
(armor clinking)

781
01:02:07.795 --> 01:02:09.263
(dramatic music)
(sword rasping)

782
01:02:09.330 --> 01:02:10.397
(birds squawking)
(brooding music)

783
01:02:17.905 --> 01:02:20.007
(knight grunting)
(armor clinking)

784
01:02:29.850 --> 01:02:31.185
(knight groaning)

785
01:02:33.220 --> 01:02:35.289
(armor clattering)
(knight continues groaning)

786
01:02:49.036 --> 01:02:51.573
(knife rasping)
(knight screaming)

787
01:02:52.607 --> 01:02:54.775
(knight coughing and gasping)
(dramatic music continues)

788
01:02:59.913 --> 01:03:01.982
(armor clinking)
(knight groaning)

789
01:03:06.020 --> 01:03:07.622
(armor clattering)

790
01:03:07.689 --> 01:03:09.423
(knight groaning)
(dramatic music continues)

791
01:03:11.458 --> 01:03:13.127
(armor clattering)

792
01:03:15.195 --> 01:03:17.464
(water splashing)

793
01:03:18.533 --> 01:03:20.602
(Morwen grunting)
(knight groaning)

794
01:03:25.139 --> 01:03:28.075
(knight coughing)
(Morwen continues grunting)

795
01:03:35.816 --> 01:03:37.918
(water splashing)
(pensive music)

796
01:03:50.565 --> 01:03:52.567
(Morwen grunts)
(knife rasping)

797
01:03:52.634 --> 01:03:57.204
(bag rustling)
(coins clinking)

798
01:03:57.271 --> 01:04:02.309
(knife rasping)
(voices whispering)

799
01:04:13.120 --> 01:04:16.023
(Morwen grunting)

800
01:04:25.032 --> 01:04:27.134
(waves lapping)
(birds chirping)

801
01:04:32.774 --> 01:04:35.175
- [Jago] What thoughts
have you in mind?

802
01:04:38.345 --> 01:04:40.914
- Just thoughts, nothing more.

803
01:04:44.118 --> 01:04:46.755
- Share them with me.
(fire crackling)

804
01:04:56.330 --> 01:04:58.065
- I think of demons.

805
01:05:00.802 --> 01:05:01.935
- [Jago] Wow.

806
01:05:04.371 --> 01:05:07.842
- Yesterday, in the
sermon, the father spoke

807
01:05:07.908 --> 01:05:09.677
of the demon Mammon,

808
01:05:12.045 --> 01:05:16.450
who lusts for earthly
pleasures and material wealth,

809
01:05:19.253 --> 01:05:21.689
and I looked on Mistress May

810
01:05:23.591 --> 01:05:26.326
happy with her newborn child

811
01:05:26.393 --> 01:05:29.764
who wears a silver cross
fashioned for his tiny neck,

812
01:05:29.831 --> 01:05:32.299
and, and I was

813
01:05:35.202 --> 01:05:39.373
filled with a terrifying greed.

814
01:05:42.777 --> 01:05:44.945
(birds chirping)
(fire crackling)

815
01:05:48.716 --> 01:05:49.983
I want what she has.

816
01:05:52.953 --> 01:05:54.556
I want her wealth,

817
01:05:57.926 --> 01:06:02.329
and her comfort, and
her happy rosy cheeks,

818
01:06:02.697 --> 01:06:04.164
and her fat baby.

819
01:06:11.305 --> 01:06:13.575
- Well, why shouldn't you?

820
01:06:18.378 --> 01:06:21.516
- Perhaps it's you
who are the demon.

821
01:06:22.717 --> 01:06:24.084
(pensive music)

822
01:06:24.151 --> 01:06:26.253
(Jago grunting)
(Anne laughs)

823
01:06:26.320 --> 01:06:28.422
(fire crackling)
(pensive music continues)

824
01:06:33.828 --> 01:06:35.763
- You thinking on him?

825
01:06:41.569 --> 01:06:44.304
- It was always the three of us,

826
01:06:47.474 --> 01:06:51.144
and now everything has
changed so suddenly.

827
01:06:53.013 --> 01:06:55.617
- Aye, everything has changed.

828
01:06:59.988 --> 01:07:00.889
Leave her.

829
01:07:02.590 --> 01:07:04.157
Come live with me.

830
01:07:08.462 --> 01:07:10.598
- I'm all she has.

831
01:07:10.665 --> 01:07:14.167
- I need a wife, and
you have no husband.

832
01:07:16.704 --> 01:07:18.305
Come live with me.

833
01:07:19.172 --> 01:07:21.174
- You don't understand.

834
01:07:24.444 --> 01:07:26.246
- But I want you now.

835
01:07:28.716 --> 01:07:31.285
(gentle music)

836
01:07:31.351 --> 01:07:33.353
- You are a greedy man.

837
01:07:41.729 --> 01:07:42.664
- Aye.

838
01:07:46.968 --> 01:07:52.040
(birds chirping)
(gentle music continues)

839
01:07:56.209 --> 01:07:58.278
(footsteps plodding)
(birds continue chirping)

840
01:08:03.317 --> 01:08:06.119
- Morwen.
(door creaking)

841
01:08:06.186 --> 01:08:07.522
I must speak with you.

842
01:08:07.589 --> 01:08:10.525
(door clattering)

843
01:08:12.292 --> 01:08:17.230
I have decided I'm going to
live with Jago and be his wife.

844
01:08:18.833 --> 01:08:20.568
This is what I want.

845
01:08:23.571 --> 01:08:24.906
Do you hear me?

846
01:08:26.440 --> 01:08:27.374
Morwen?

847
01:08:29.409 --> 01:08:32.747
I have always obeyed
you in all things.

848
01:08:34.082 --> 01:08:35.717
I followed your commands

849
01:08:35.783 --> 01:08:39.887
even when the things you
did made my stomach turn.

850
01:08:41.254 --> 01:08:44.559
I was content to
stay by your side.

851
01:08:44.626 --> 01:08:47.095
You were my husband's mother.

852
01:08:50.230 --> 01:08:51.633
But Seamus is gone.

853
01:08:51.699 --> 01:08:54.234
(dramatic music)
- Don't say his name,

854
01:08:54.301 --> 01:08:55.402
slut, whore.

855
01:08:57.538 --> 01:09:00.407
You'll burn with
the rest of them.

856
01:09:00.474 --> 01:09:03.343
Don't you see what you're doing?

857
01:09:03.410 --> 01:09:04.912
- Morwen, I-

858
01:09:04.979 --> 01:09:08.549
- You'll abandon me and
condemn me to death,

859
01:09:08.616 --> 01:09:11.819
and the knights of
hell will come for you,

860
01:09:11.886 --> 01:09:14.822
and I will cheer for them.

861
01:09:14.889 --> 01:09:19.961
You cannot abandon your duty
to me without consequences.

862
01:09:20.962 --> 01:09:22.630
They will pull you down to hell.

863
01:09:25.432 --> 01:09:27.467
(Anne whimpering)
(dramatic music continues)

864
01:09:34.742 --> 01:09:36.778
(footsteps plodding)
(brooding music)

865
01:09:43.017 --> 01:09:46.020
- I won't live under
her thumb, (gasping)

866
01:09:46.087 --> 01:09:48.156
not for one more moment.

867
01:09:49.356 --> 01:09:51.125
I'll do what I want.

868
01:09:58.966 --> 01:10:01.669
(wind howling)

869
01:10:09.977 --> 01:10:12.814
(brooding music)

870
01:10:29.564 --> 01:10:32.365
(brooding music continues)

871
01:10:35.536 --> 01:10:37.370
(dramatic music)
(armor clattering)

872
01:10:38.405 --> 01:10:40.608
(sword rasping)

873
01:10:41.374 --> 01:10:42.577
I'm sorry.

874
01:10:42.643 --> 01:10:44.112
(air whooshing)
(sword rasping)

875
01:10:44.178 --> 01:10:48.082
(Anne inhales and exhales)
(fire crackling)

876
01:11:00.762 --> 01:11:02.262
(birds squawking)
(fire continues crackling)

877
01:11:06.534 --> 01:11:07.969
(birds chirping)

878
01:11:08.035 --> 01:11:08.936
(Jago sniffs)

879
01:11:10.538 --> 01:11:13.040
- [Jago] It's cold and early,

880
01:11:15.610 --> 01:11:18.713
too early. (coughs)

881
01:11:20.681 --> 01:11:22.984
- Today is Sunday.
- Is it?

882
01:11:26.621 --> 01:11:29.824
- Come to the sermon
this afternoon with me.

883
01:11:31.592 --> 01:11:34.796
God's words will
soothe your soul.

884
01:11:34.862 --> 01:11:37.397
(Jago laughs)

885
01:11:37.464 --> 01:11:40.134
(gentle music)

886
01:11:47.074 --> 01:11:50.077
- You think my soul
needs soothing?

887
01:11:53.714 --> 01:11:56.284
- I will make you a pious man.

888
01:12:04.625 --> 01:12:07.795
- May it please you
to prosper, Zion,

889
01:12:09.329 --> 01:12:12.300
to build up the
walls of Jerusalem.

890
01:12:13.935 --> 01:12:17.271
Then you will delight
in the sacrifices

891
01:12:18.438 --> 01:12:19.841
of the righteous

892
01:12:22.743 --> 01:12:25.546
in burnt offerings
offered whole.

893
01:12:27.315 --> 01:12:30.818
Then bulls will be
offered on your altar.

894
01:12:33.353 --> 01:12:35.455
(feet thudding)
(pensive music continues)

895
01:12:40.928 --> 01:12:42.462
(priest singing in Latin)

896
01:12:59.180 --> 01:13:01.916
(waves lapping)

897
01:13:01.983 --> 01:13:04.952
- [Children] <i>The fox and his</i>
<i>wife, without any strife,</i>

898
01:13:05.019 --> 01:13:07.922
<i>cut the goose with</i>
<i>a fork and knife.</i>

899
01:13:07.989 --> 01:13:10.625
<i>They never had such</i>
<i>supper in their life.</i>

900
01:13:10.691 --> 01:13:12.326
<i>The little ones</i>
<i>chewed on the bones,</i>

901
01:13:12.425 --> 01:13:14.394
<i>the bones, the bones.</i>

902
01:13:14.461 --> 01:13:15.830
(bodies thudding)
(children laughing)

903
01:13:15.897 --> 01:13:18.132
(waves lapping)
(gentle music)

904
01:13:18.199 --> 01:13:20.101
- You failed us. I win.

905
01:13:20.167 --> 01:13:21.736
- I did not.
- You're a liar.

906
01:13:21.802 --> 01:13:23.436
- Stop. It was me.

907
01:13:23.503 --> 01:13:24.739
I failed us.

908
01:13:24.805 --> 01:13:27.808
(fist thudding)
(Jago groans)

909
01:13:27.875 --> 01:13:30.945
(pensive music)
(waves lapping)

910
01:13:34.382 --> 01:13:36.416
(footsteps plodding)
(waves continue lapping)

911
01:13:42.857 --> 01:13:46.093
(pensive music)

912
01:13:46.160 --> 01:13:49.297
(footsteps plodding)

913
01:13:51.899 --> 01:13:53.901
- Come on. Sun is down.

914
01:13:55.169 --> 01:13:56.570
We should leave.

915
01:13:57.738 --> 01:14:00.675
- Just a small prayer for Morwen

916
01:14:00.741 --> 01:14:02.076
and for Seamus.

917
01:14:05.179 --> 01:14:08.481
- Seamus is dead
and in the dirt.

918
01:14:08.549 --> 01:14:09.550
I told you.

919
01:14:11.252 --> 01:14:13.287
Rotherham's men smashed his
head in, left him to die,

920
01:14:13.354 --> 01:14:17.091
and I don't want to
hear any more about him.

921
01:14:19.560 --> 01:14:24.464
- I thought it was the thieves
who split him neck to navel.

922
01:14:31.906 --> 01:14:35.309
- What does it matter,
Anne? Man's gone.

923
01:14:36.444 --> 01:14:38.746
(pensive music)

924
01:14:38.813 --> 01:14:40.581
They found our camp.

925
01:14:42.482 --> 01:14:44.418
Seamus tried to fight.

926
01:14:47.388 --> 01:14:48.990
(air whooshing)

927
01:14:49.056 --> 01:14:50.624
And he was a fool.

928
01:14:54.595 --> 01:14:55.495
- Tell me.

929
01:14:56.897 --> 01:14:59.200
You must tell me the truth.

930
01:15:02.737 --> 01:15:03.637
- Truth?

931
01:15:11.946 --> 01:15:14.515
I have always loved you, Anne.

932
01:15:15.416 --> 01:15:17.218
Do you not know that?

933
01:15:18.586 --> 01:15:21.322
And now you can be
mine, truly mine.

934
01:15:24.125 --> 01:15:28.029
We can leave Seamus
behind, his mother behind.

935
01:15:31.599 --> 01:15:33.901
Our lives are ours to live.

936
01:15:35.836 --> 01:15:38.339
We don't owe anyone anything.

937
01:15:41.475 --> 01:15:46.213
- Tell me the truth, or I
will never speak to you again.

938
01:15:47.648 --> 01:15:50.217
(pensive music continues)

939
01:15:57.792 --> 01:16:01.195
- He changed while we was away.

940
01:16:05.566 --> 01:16:08.235
His ambition, it grew and grew,

941
01:16:10.539 --> 01:16:12.339
and he was unafraid.

942
01:16:12.406 --> 01:16:13.274
(clothes rustling)

943
01:16:13.340 --> 01:16:14.675
- Seamus, don't.

944
01:16:16.210 --> 01:16:19.280
(knife rasping)
(soldier groans)

945
01:16:19.346 --> 01:16:23.250
- [Jago] War bred in him
(knife rasping)

946
01:16:23.317 --> 01:16:24.385
an appetite.

947
01:16:25.753 --> 01:16:28.823
- (whistling) Come
before it gets too dark.

948
01:16:28.889 --> 01:16:32.993
(clothes rustling)
(Seamus gasping)

949
01:16:33.060 --> 01:16:34.995
He's got a purse on him.

950
01:16:35.062 --> 01:16:37.264
(bag rustling)

951
01:16:38.332 --> 01:16:40.234
What's wrong with you?

952
01:16:42.403 --> 01:16:43.304
Huh?

953
01:16:44.438 --> 01:16:46.207
(strap snaps)
(coins clinking)

954
01:16:48.242 --> 01:16:50.478
Scared of a dead man, huh?

955
01:16:50.545 --> 01:16:53.147
(coins clinking)
(Seamus laughs)

956
01:16:53.214 --> 01:16:56.117
(Seamus exhaling)

957
01:16:57.885 --> 01:16:59.554
(horse neighing)

958
01:16:59.620 --> 01:17:04.725
(birds squawking)
(brooding music)

959
01:17:17.238 --> 01:17:19.306
(metal clanging)
(leaves rustling)

960
01:17:30.818 --> 01:17:32.019
(creature growling)

961
01:17:32.086 --> 01:17:33.721
(fist thudding)
(soldier groans)

962
01:17:33.787 --> 01:17:35.689
(creature growling)

963
01:17:35.756 --> 01:17:38.926
(dramatic music)
(fighters grunting)

964
01:17:39.994 --> 01:17:42.763
(hands thudding)

965
01:17:46.333 --> 01:17:49.604
(knife thudding)
(Seamus screaming)

966
01:17:49.670 --> 01:17:51.540
(knife rasping)
(Seamus grunts)

967
01:17:51.606 --> 01:17:54.441
(knight gagging)

968
01:18:00.915 --> 01:18:02.950
(hand thudding)
(creature continues growling)

969
01:18:03.984 --> 01:18:06.020
(knife rasping)
(Seamus grunting)

970
01:18:08.088 --> 01:18:10.824
(pensive music)

971
01:18:16.497 --> 01:18:19.200
(cloth rustling)

972
01:18:19.601 --> 01:18:22.604
(Morwen grunting)

973
01:18:22.671 --> 01:18:25.507
(Morwen gasping)

974
01:18:30.545 --> 01:18:32.146
(pensive music continues)

975
01:18:37.718 --> 01:18:39.820
(voices whispering)
(brooding music)

976
01:18:43.658 --> 01:18:45.125
(helmet clattering)

977
01:18:45.192 --> 01:18:48.062
(Morwen grunting)
(voices whispering)

978
01:18:50.965 --> 01:18:52.967
(helmet clattering)

979
01:18:53.033 --> 01:18:55.836
(Morwen grunting)

980
01:18:55.903 --> 01:18:58.005
(Morwen gasps)
(pensive music)

981
01:19:02.243 --> 01:19:05.079
(knees thudding)

982
01:19:05.145 --> 01:19:07.748
(Morwen whimpering)

983
01:19:07.815 --> 01:19:08.717
- No.

984
01:19:10.184 --> 01:19:13.622
- Seamus, don't.

985
01:19:16.890 --> 01:19:20.227
- Seamus. (whimpering)

986
01:19:24.932 --> 01:19:26.433
(creature growling)

987
01:19:26.500 --> 01:19:28.435
(armor clattering)

988
01:19:33.907 --> 01:19:37.444
You came back to me. (sobbing)

989
01:19:45.386 --> 01:19:47.121
You came back to me.

990
01:19:49.123 --> 01:19:50.124
Ah, Seamus.

991
01:19:52.192 --> 01:19:54.261
(fire crackling)
(brooding music)

992
01:20:00.434 --> 01:20:02.503
(voices whispering)
(brooding music continues)

993
01:20:08.809 --> 01:20:11.145
(creature growling)

994
01:20:11.211 --> 01:20:13.615
(dramatic music)
(Seamus screaming)

995
01:20:14.649 --> 01:20:16.751
(hands thudding)
(Seamus continues screaming)

996
01:20:24.425 --> 01:20:27.828
- [Seamus] Help.
It won't come off.

997
01:20:27.895 --> 01:20:29.963
(Seamus screaming)
(fire crackling)

998
01:20:34.835 --> 01:20:37.605
- [Jago] I really had no choice.

999
01:20:39.607 --> 01:20:41.141
(Anne exhales)
(pensive music)

1000
01:20:44.178 --> 01:20:46.113
- You left him behind.

1001
01:20:47.582 --> 01:20:50.785
- (sighs) I had no choice.

1002
01:20:50.851 --> 01:20:52.687
(Anne exhales)

1003
01:20:52.754 --> 01:20:54.689
- Morwen was right.

1004
01:20:54.756 --> 01:20:56.691
You always were a jealous boy.

1005
01:20:56.758 --> 01:20:58.892
- Stay.
- Let go of me.

1006
01:20:58.959 --> 01:21:01.028
(footsteps plodding)
(wind howling)

1007
01:21:05.466 --> 01:21:07.201
(footsteps plodding)
(crickets chirping)

1008
01:21:07.267 --> 01:21:10.371
(Anne sighs)
(footsteps continue plodding)

1009
01:21:15.209 --> 01:21:18.546
(pensive music)
(wind howling)

1010
01:21:22.517 --> 01:21:24.753
(footsteps plodding)

1011
01:21:31.793 --> 01:21:32.694
Father.

1012
01:21:35.062 --> 01:21:35.929
Father?

1013
01:21:42.537 --> 01:21:44.104
(voices whispering)
(Anne gasps)

1014
01:21:47.174 --> 01:21:49.744
(eerie music)

1015
01:21:52.179 --> 01:21:53.848
No, leave me alone.

1016
01:21:55.082 --> 01:21:57.184
(knight exhales)
(voices whispering)

1017
01:22:01.355 --> 01:22:02.690
Leave me alone.

1018
01:22:03.924 --> 01:22:05.593
(dramatic music)
(hooves clopping)

1019
01:22:05.660 --> 01:22:07.428
(animals screeching)
(hooves continue clopping)

1020
01:22:14.034 --> 01:22:15.637
(footsteps plodding)
(pensive music)

1021
01:22:15.703 --> 01:22:17.204
(hand knocking)

1022
01:22:17.271 --> 01:22:18.873
Morwen, let me in.

1023
01:22:19.841 --> 01:22:21.975
We, we are not safe here.

1024
01:22:22.042 --> 01:22:24.278
(door creaking)
(rain pattering)

1025
01:22:26.346 --> 01:22:27.247
Morwen.

1026
01:22:30.250 --> 01:22:33.086
(grass rustling)

1027
01:22:40.394 --> 01:22:42.429
(rain pattering)
(pensive music continues)

1028
01:22:53.440 --> 01:22:54.308
(dramatic music)

1029
01:22:54.374 --> 01:22:55.810
(Anne screaming)

1030
01:22:55.877 --> 01:22:58.947
- [Morwen] Anne, Anne,
Anne, get it off.

1031
01:23:01.215 --> 01:23:02.684
Anne, Anne, help.

1032
01:23:05.452 --> 01:23:08.222
Help me. I can't get it off.

1033
01:23:08.288 --> 01:23:09.691
- Morwen.

1034
01:23:09.757 --> 01:23:13.494
- [Morwen] (groans)
Anne, please.

1035
01:23:13.561 --> 01:23:16.163
- Are you trying to scare
me back into submission?

1036
01:23:16.230 --> 01:23:17.998
- [Morwen] Have pity on me.

1037
01:23:18.065 --> 01:23:19.333
- So I come back to your side.
- I can't get it off.

1038
01:23:19.399 --> 01:23:20.535
It hurts.

1039
01:23:20.602 --> 01:23:22.002
- You're being foolish.

1040
01:23:22.069 --> 01:23:23.504
- [Morwen] No.
(fire roaring)

1041
01:23:23.571 --> 01:23:25.172
(screams) No, it's
stuck, it's stuck.

1042
01:23:25.239 --> 01:23:26.508
Horrible.
(fire roaring)

1043
01:23:26.574 --> 01:23:27.775
Horrible, horrible.

1044
01:23:27.842 --> 01:23:29.443
Get it off, get it off.

1045
01:23:29.511 --> 01:23:33.247
- Hold still.
- God, Anne, it's hurting me.

1046
01:23:33.313 --> 01:23:37.685
(Morwen screaming)
(Anne gasping)

1047
01:23:37.752 --> 01:23:38.720
Anne, Anne.

1048
01:23:40.454 --> 01:23:43.457
(door squeaking)
(feet pattering)

1049
01:23:43.525 --> 01:23:45.025
(pensive music)

1050
01:23:45.092 --> 01:23:47.394
(cross clattering)

1051
01:23:47.461 --> 01:23:48.462
Anne, Anne.

1052
01:23:49.664 --> 01:23:51.031
- Be still.

1053
01:23:51.098 --> 01:23:52.399
- [Morwen] (screams)
No, I'm afraid.

1054
01:23:52.466 --> 01:23:54.602
- There's nothing
to be afraid of.

1055
01:23:54.669 --> 01:23:57.605
(cross thuds)
(helmet clattering)

1056
01:23:57.672 --> 01:24:02.710
(rain pattering)
(Morwen groaning and sobbing)

1057
01:24:03.377 --> 01:24:05.680
(pensive music)

1058
01:24:08.516 --> 01:24:09.684
- I need you.

1059
01:24:13.120 --> 01:24:14.022
Please.

1060
01:24:16.891 --> 01:24:18.225
I'm sorry.

1061
01:24:18.292 --> 01:24:22.462
(Anne breathing heavily)

1062
01:24:22.530 --> 01:24:25.033
- Now you really are a demon.

1063
01:24:26.834 --> 01:24:28.736
- [Morwen] Forgive me.

1064
01:24:31.138 --> 01:24:32.105
Forgive me.

1065
01:24:34.742 --> 01:24:35.677
- No way.

1066
01:24:36.911 --> 01:24:38.713
(Morwen whimpering)
(rain pattering)

1067
01:24:42.382 --> 01:24:43.751
(metal clanging)

1068
01:24:43.818 --> 01:24:46.788
(voices whispering)
(fire crackling)

1069
01:24:53.427 --> 01:24:55.329
(air whooshing)

1070
01:24:55.395 --> 01:24:57.230
Ah, come, come, come.

1071
01:24:58.265 --> 01:25:00.935
(wind howling)

1072
01:25:04.072 --> 01:25:07.240
Here.
(pensive music)

1073
01:25:09.343 --> 01:25:11.012
(table clattering)

1074
01:25:11.079 --> 01:25:13.146
(Anne gasping)
(rain pattering)

1075
01:25:17.284 --> 01:25:19.252
(hand thudding)

1076
01:25:20.922 --> 01:25:23.758
(brooding music)

1077
01:25:26.594 --> 01:25:28.395
(air whooshing)

1078
01:25:31.733 --> 01:25:34.569
(rain pattering)

1079
01:25:35.937 --> 01:25:38.973
(hand thudding)
(brooding music continues)

1080
01:25:46.948 --> 01:25:49.017
(Morwen whimpering)
(pensive music)

1081
01:25:52.553 --> 01:25:53.420
Shh.

1082
01:25:56.924 --> 01:25:58.760
Shh.
(pensive music continues)

1083
01:26:03.430 --> 01:26:05.667
(table clattering)

1084
01:26:09.570 --> 01:26:11.639
(door clattering and creaking)
(pensive music continues)

1085
01:26:26.453 --> 01:26:28.523
(voices whispering)

1086
01:26:34.996 --> 01:26:38.198
(helmet clanking)
(voices continue whispering)

1087
01:26:38.265 --> 01:26:40.601
- [Morwen] It's
cursed. Don't touch it.

1088
01:26:40.668 --> 01:26:42.737
(voices whispering)
(pensive music continues)

1089
01:26:48.643 --> 01:26:49.544
- No.

1090
01:26:52.379 --> 01:26:54.481
It has no power over me.

1091
01:27:02.023 --> 01:27:03.758
(Morwen whimpering)
(pensive music continues)

1092
01:27:05.827 --> 01:27:08.062
There is nothing to fear.

1093
01:27:14.902 --> 01:27:17.004
(waves lapping)
(pensive music continues)

1094
01:27:21.241 --> 01:27:23.945
(birds chirping)
(waves continue lapping)

1095
01:27:29.650 --> 01:27:30.885
- [Jago] Anne.

1096
01:27:32.720 --> 01:27:34.789
Wait.
- What do you want?

1097
01:27:38.425 --> 01:27:40.995
- I was looking for you.

1098
01:27:41.062 --> 01:27:42.797
I couldn't find you.

1099
01:27:43.865 --> 01:27:45.465
- What do you want?

1100
01:27:47.001 --> 01:27:49.070
- You, Anne, I want you.

1101
01:27:50.938 --> 01:27:54.041
(waves lapping)
(gentle music)

1102
01:27:57.078 --> 01:27:59.279
- I will not be yours or hers.

1103
01:28:01.949 --> 01:28:04.451
I don't belong to anyone.

1104
01:28:08.122 --> 01:28:11.526
- All your talk of demons, Anne,

1105
01:28:11.592 --> 01:28:13.995
I'm not the one hurting you.

1106
01:28:15.362 --> 01:28:18.331
(clothes rustling)

1107
01:28:19.233 --> 01:28:20.134
Come back.

1108
01:28:22.036 --> 01:28:22.937
Anne.

1109
01:28:25.039 --> 01:28:27.575
Go then. Hag.

1110
01:28:32.046 --> 01:28:34.782
(waves lapping)

1111
01:28:37.652 --> 01:28:40.888
(birds chirping)
(wind howling)

1112
01:28:40.955 --> 01:28:44.125
(footsteps plodding)

1113
01:28:50.330 --> 01:28:51.599
- Come inside.

1114
01:28:52.633 --> 01:28:54.001
(door clattering and creaking)

1115
01:29:01.642 --> 01:29:04.178
Here.
(pestle thudding)

1116
01:29:04.245 --> 01:29:07.548
This will help you sleep.
(liquid sloshing)

1117
01:29:07.615 --> 01:29:10.685
I'll be back before
the sun is down.

1118
01:29:11.786 --> 01:29:13.588
- [Morwen] Yes, Anne.

1119
01:29:13.654 --> 01:29:16.724
(door creaking and clattering)

1120
01:29:16.791 --> 01:29:19.760
(footsteps plodding)

1121
01:29:19.827 --> 01:29:21.896
(birds chirping)
(wind howling)

1122
01:29:26.366 --> 01:29:29.469
(voices whispering)
(pensive music)

1123
01:29:44.451 --> 01:29:46.520
(chain clinking)
(voices continue whispering)

1124
01:29:57.064 --> 01:29:59.166
(lid clattering)
(voices continue whispering)

1125
01:30:16.651 --> 01:30:18.719
(voices continue whispering)

1126
01:30:29.664 --> 01:30:32.400
(pensive music continues)

1127
01:31:39.633 --> 01:31:43.204
(pensive music continues)

1128
01:31:59.620 --> 01:32:03.190
(pensive music continues)

1129
01:32:19.774 --> 01:32:23.344
(pensive music continues)

1130
01:32:39.660 --> 01:32:43.230
(pensive music continues)

1131
01:33:37.586 --> 01:33:40.054
(waves lapping)

1132
01:33:42.022 --> 01:33:44.725
♪ <i>Merry it is while</i>
<i>summer it lasts</i> ♪

1133
01:33:44.859 --> 01:33:47.695
♪ <i>With song of birds</i> ♪

1134
01:33:48.762 --> 01:33:53.834
♪ <i>But now draws near the wind's</i>
<i>blast and harsh weather</i> ♪

1135
01:33:55.102 --> 01:33:58.739
♪ <i>Aye, aye, aye,</i>
<i>this night is long</i> ♪

1136
01:33:58.873 --> 01:34:02.776
♪ <i>And I most unjustly</i> ♪

1137
01:34:02.910 --> 01:34:06.147
♪ <i>Sorrow, and mourn, and fast</i> ♪
